+## Room Memberships
+
+- Human users automatically join all open rooms (`Rooms::Open`) on creation and when a room is created as or converted to `Rooms::Open`.
+- Bots do **not** join open rooms by default (`auto_join_open_rooms: false`).
+- When `"Add to all open rooms"` (`auto_join_open_rooms: true`) is enabled on a bot (at creation or on update):
+  - `after_save_commit :grant_membership_to_open_rooms` grants the bot membership to all existing `Rooms::Open`.
+  - Any `Rooms::Open` created later or converted from `Rooms::Closed` grants membership to `User.active.auto_joining_open_rooms` (all active non-bot users plus active bots with `auto_join_open_rooms: true`).
+  - Turning `"Add to all open rooms"` off preserves the bot's existing room memberships.
+- Bots can be individually added to or removed from open rooms (`Rooms::OpensController`) and closed rooms (`Rooms::ClosedsController`) via the `"Give <bot name> access to this room"` switch, and can be added to direct rooms (`Rooms::Direct`).
+- Bots in a room appear in `@`-mention autocomplete (`/autocompletable/users`) alongside human users.
